module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatEquivalence
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatEquivalenceConverse
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The local equational criterion for flatness: flatness implies the criterion

Let `(C, O)` be a ringed site and let `F` be a sheaf of `O`-modules. Stacks 08FC characterises
flatness of `F` by a local factorisation property of the relations among its sections. Parts (2)
and (3) of the source — one relation at a time versus a finite matrix of relations — are proved
equivalent in `StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatRelations`, and the substrate for
the remaining equivalence is built in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatEquivalence`.

This file proves the direction **(1) implies (2)**: a flat sheaf of modules satisfies the
single-relation criterion. The converse, (2) implies (1), is proved in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatCriterionConverse`, which is also where the
equivalence of (1) and (2) is stated.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.hasLocalSingleRelationFactorizations_of_isFlat`: a flat sheaf of
  `O`-modules satisfies the single-relation local factorisation criterion.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyInjective_tensorRight_map_of_isFlat`: the form in which
  flatness is used, and the only place it is used — tensoring with a flat sheaf of modules takes
  a *locally* injective morphism of *presheaves* of modules to a *locally* injective morphism.
  Flatness gives exactness of the sheaf-level tensor functor, which is tensoring followed by
  sheafification; the sheafification is undone by the two local bijections supplied by the units
  of the sheafification adjunction.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.relElt`, `relElt_restrict` and `tensorRight_map_ι_relElt`: the element
  `∑ aᵢ ⊗ sᵢ` of the relation subpresheaf tensored with `F`, its restrictions, and the fact that
  the inclusion of the relation subpresheaf annihilates it. This is the point at which the
  relation `∑ aᵢ • sᵢ = 0` is consumed.

## Implementation notes

**The proof.** Stacks works on the localised site `C/U` with the sheaf of ideals generated by
`a₁, …, a_n`; this file instead works on `C` with the extension by zero of that ideal sheaf,
realised as `Stacks.SheafOfModules.relSubmodule a`, a subpresheaf of the free presheaf of
`O`-modules on `Hom(-, U)`. The element `∑ᵢ relGen a (𝟙 U) i ⊗ sᵢ` of
`relSubmodule a ⊗ F` is killed by the inclusion `relSubmodule a ⟶ freeOn O U` tensored with `F`,
because there it becomes `freeMk (𝟙 U) ⊗ (∑ᵢ aᵢ • sᵢ) = freeMk (𝟙 U) ⊗ 0`. Flatness makes that
inclusion locally injective after tensoring, so the element vanishes on a covering sieve of `U`,
and on each member the local algebraic step `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_relFactorization`
(Mathlib's equational criterion for the vanishing of a tensor, Stacks 04VX) produces the
factorisation.

**One spelling for the underlying presheaf of rings.** The objectwise tensor product is stated
over `Stacks.ringPresheaf O.obj` and `SheafOfModules` over `(Stacks.commRingSheafToRingSheaf
O).obj`. The two are equal by `rfl`, but crossing between them at the level of *morphisms* is
what makes `rw` motives fail to typecheck at `implicit` transparency and makes instance search
miss hypotheses that are visibly present. The whole file is therefore written in the
`Stacks.ringPresheaf O.obj` spelling: `Stacks.SheafOfModules.ringUnit` is the identity read as a
morphism between the two spellings, and `shfR`, `shfRightR`, `shfAdjR`, `valR` re-spell
sheafification, its right adjoint, its adjunction and the underlying presheaf of a sheaf. These
are *re-spellings*, not reimplementations: each is a one-line application of the Mathlib
construction, and `shf`, `shfRight`, `shfAdj` of `FlatEquivalence` are definitionally the same
functors. The single crossing to the sheaf-level tensor functor of flatness is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.mono_shf_map_tensorRightOf_map_val`.

Two further consequences of the same fact: every equation between morphisms used
as a rewrite rule here has its type **written out**, because an equation obtained from
`Functor.map_comp` with its arguments inferred records a different (though definitionally equal)
intermediate object and then `rw` reports "did not find an occurrence" against a goal that
prints identically; and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyInjective_comp_addCommGrp`
takes both factors as explicit arguments, because
`CategoryTheory.Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_comp` is an instance and instance search does not
find the two factors when they are local hypotheses of a composite built by unification.

**Universes.** The sections of the structure sheaf live in `max v w`, not an independent
universe, exactly as in `FlatEquivalence`: the free presheaf there is free on the index set
`V ⟶ U`, which lives in the morphism universe `v`, so its sections live in `max v w`. The
narrowing is inherited from that file, is forced by the construction rather than chosen, and is
the only universe constraint here. Stacks 08FC states its ringed site with three independent
universes; this is where the difference comes from.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08FC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08FC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04VX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04VX)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe w v u

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

section Helper

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)

/-- Composition of two locally injective morphisms of presheaves of abelian groups, with both
hypotheses taken as explicit arguments.  `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_comp` is
an instance, and in the situations below the two factors are themselves local hypotheses that
instance search does not pick up. -/
lemma isLocallyInjective_comp_addCommGrp {F₁ F₂ F₃ : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{max v w}}
    (φ : F₁ ⟶ F₂) (ψ : F₂ ⟶ F₃)
    (h₁ : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J φ) (h₂ : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J ψ) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J (φ ≫ ψ) :=
  let := h₁
  let := h₂
  inferInstance

/-- If `u ≫ e = e' ≫ w` with `e'` and `w` locally injective, then `u` is locally injective. -/
private theorem isLocallyInjective_of_comp_eq_comp
    {F₁ F₂ F₃ F₄ : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{max v w}} (u : F₁ ⟶ F₂) (e : F₂ ⟶ F₄) (e' : F₁ ⟶ F₃)
    (w : F₃ ⟶ F₄) (h : u ≫ e = e' ≫ w) (h₁ : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J e')
    (h₂ : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J w) : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J u :=
  let := isLocallyInjective_comp_addCommGrp J _ _ h₁ h₂
  Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_of_isLocallyInjective_fac J h

end Helper

section Spelling

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{max v w} RingCat.{max v w})]

/-- The identity, read as a morphism from `Stacks.ringPresheaf O.obj` — the spelling of the
underlying presheaf of rings that the objectwise tensor product uses — to the underlying
presheaf of `Stacks.commRingSheafToRingSheaf O`, which is the spelling `SheafOfModules` uses.
Every statement below is written with this one morphism, so that the two spellings meet in
exactly one place. -/
noncomputable def ringUnit (O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{max v w}) :
    ringPresheaf O.obj ⟶ (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj :=
  𝟙 _

variable (O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{max v w})

/-- The identity `Stacks.SheafOfModules.ringUnit` is locally injective. -/
instance isLocallyInjective_ringUnit : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J (ringUnit O) :=
  Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_of_injective J _ (fun _ _ _ h ↦ h)

/-- The identity `Stacks.SheafOfModules.ringUnit` is locally surjective. -/
instance isLocallySurjective_ringUnit : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (ringUnit O) :=
  Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_of_surjective J _ (fun _ x ↦ ⟨x, rfl⟩)

/-- The right adjoint of sheafification acts on morphisms by taking the underlying morphism of
presheaves of modules. -/
lemma shfRightR_map_eq
    {M N : _root_.SheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)} (u : M ⟶ N) :
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.forget (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O) ⋙
      PresheafOfModules.restrictScalars (ringUnit O)).map u = u.val := by
  apply PresheafOfModules.hom_ext
  intro X
  rfl

variable [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max v w}]
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max v w}]

/-- Sheafification of presheaves of `O`-modules, with its source spelled
`Stacks.ringPresheaf O.obj`. -/
noncomputable abbrev shfR :
    PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj) ⥤
      _root_.SheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O) :=
  PresheafOfModules.sheafification (ringUnit O)

/-- The right adjoint of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.shfR`. -/
noncomputable abbrev shfRightR :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O) ⥤
      PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj) :=
  _root_.SheafOfModules.forget (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O) ⋙
    PresheafOfModules.restrictScalars (ringUnit O)

/-- The sheafification adjunction, in the `Stacks.ringPresheaf O.obj` spelling. -/
noncomputable abbrev shfAdjR : shfR O ⊣ shfRightR O :=
  PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction (ringUnit O)

variable {O}

/-- The unit of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.shfAdjR` is locally injective. -/
instance isLocallyInjective_shfAdjR_unit
    (P : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map ((shfAdjR O).unit.app P)) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J P.presheaf))

/-- The unit of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.shfAdjR` is locally surjective. -/
instance isLocallySurjective_shfAdjR_unit
    (P : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map ((shfAdjR O).unit.app P)) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J P.presheaf))

/-- The underlying presheaf of modules of a sheaf of `O`-modules, in the
`Stacks.ringPresheaf O.obj` spelling. -/
noncomputable abbrev valR (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)) :
    PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj) :=
  F.val

/-- A morphism of presheaves of modules whose sheafification is a monomorphism is locally
injective. -/
lemma isLocallyInjective_of_mono_shfR_map
    {P Q : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)} (u : P ⟶ Q)
    (hu : Mono ((shfR O).map u)) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map u) := by
  have h1 : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map ((shfRightR O).map ((shfR O).map u))) :=
    Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_of_injective _ _
      (fun X ↦ injective_val_app_of_mono ((shfR O).map u) X)
  refine isLocallyInjective_of_comp_eq_comp J _
    ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map ((shfAdjR O).unit.app Q)) _ _ ?_
    (isLocallyInjective_shfAdjR_unit P) h1
  simp only [← Functor.map_comp]
  exact congrArg _ ((shfAdjR O).unit.naturality u)

end Spelling

section Flat

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{max v w} RingCat.{max v w})]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max v w}]
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max v w}]
  {O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{max v w}}

/-- Tensoring the unit of the sheafification adjunction by a sheaf of modules gives a locally
injective morphism. -/
lemma isLocallyInjective_tensorRight_map_shfAdjR_unit
    (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O))
    (P : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map
        ((tensorRightOf O F).map ((shfAdjR O).unit.app P))) :=
  Stacks.isLocallyInjective_tensorRight_map (O := O.obj)
    (R := commRingSheafToRingSheaf O) (ringUnit O) F.val ((shfAdjR O).unit.app P)

/-- Tensoring with a flat sheaf of modules takes a locally injective morphism of presheaves of
modules to a locally injective morphism.

Local injectivity, rather than injectivity, is all that is needed of `u`: flatness is used
through `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mono_shf_map_of_isLocallyInjective`, which turns local
injectivity of a morphism of presheaves of modules into a monomorphism after sheafification.
A monomorphism of presheaves of modules is injective on sections, hence locally injective, so
this also covers the monomorphism case. -/
lemma isLocallyInjective_tensorRight_map_of_isFlat
    {F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)}
    (hF : IsFlat F)
    {P Q : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)} (u : P ⟶ Q)
    (hu : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map u)) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map u)) := by
  have hu' : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj).map u) := hu
  have hmonoshf : Mono ((shfR O).map u) :=
    mono_shf_map_of_isLocallyInjective (R := commRingSheafToRingSheaf O) u
  have hmono : Mono ((shfR O).map
      ((tensorRightOf O F).map ((shfR O).map u).val)) :=
    mono_shf_map_tensorRightOf_map_val hF ((shfR O).map u)
  have h1 := isLocallyInjective_of_mono_shfR_map
    ((tensorRightOf O F).map ((shfR O).map u).val) hmono
  have h2 := isLocallyInjective_tensorRight_map_shfAdjR_unit F P
  have hnat : u ≫ (shfAdjR O).unit.app Q
      = (shfAdjR O).unit.app P ≫ ((shfR O).map u).val := by
    have h : u ≫ (shfAdjR O).unit.app Q
        = (shfAdjR O).unit.app P ≫ (shfRightR O).map ((shfR O).map u) :=
      (shfAdjR O).unit.naturality u
    rw [shfRightR_map_eq] at h
    exact h
  refine isLocallyInjective_of_comp_eq_comp J _
    ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map ((shfAdjR O).unit.app Q)))
    _ _ ?_ h2 h1
  simp only [← Functor.map_comp, hnat]
  exact (congrArg _ (Functor.map_comp _ _ _)).trans (Functor.map_comp _ _ _)

end Flat


section Element

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{max v w} RingCat.{max v w})]
  {O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{max v w}}

/-- The relation element: the sum `∑ relGen a (𝟙 U) i ⊗ s i` inside the objectwise tensor
product of the relation subpresheaf with `F`. -/
noncomputable def relElt {U : C} {n : ℕ} (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    {F : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)} (s : Fin n → F.obj (op U)) :
    (tensorObj ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules) F).obj (op U) :=
  ∑ i : Fin n, (⟨relGen a (op U) (𝟙 U) i, relGen_mem a (op U) (𝟙 U) i⟩ :
      ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op U)) ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)] s i

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{max v w} RingCat.{max v w})] in
/-- Restriction takes the `𝟙 U`-generator of the relation subpresheaf to the `f`-generator. -/
lemma relSubmodule_map_relGen {U V : C} (f : V ⟶ U) {n : ℕ}
    (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)) (i : Fin n) :
    ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).map f.op
        (⟨relGen a (op U) (𝟙 U) i, relGen_mem a (op U) (𝟙 U) i⟩ :
          ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op U))
      = (⟨relGen a (op V) f i, relGen_mem a (op V) f i⟩ :
          ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op V)) := by
  refine Subtype.ext ?_
  show (freeOn O U).map f.op (relGen a (op U) (𝟙 U) i) = relGen a (op V) f i
  rw [freeOn_map_relGen, Category.comp_id]
  rfl

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{max v w} RingCat.{max v w})] in
/-- The restriction of the relation element along `f : V ⟶ U`. -/
lemma relElt_restrict {U V : C} (f : V ⟶ U) {n : ℕ}
    (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    {F : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)} (s : Fin n → F.obj (op U)) :
    (tensorObj ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules) F).map f.op (relElt a s)
      = ∑ i : Fin n, (⟨relGen a (op V) f i, relGen_mem a (op V) f i⟩ :
          ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op V))
            ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op V)] F.map f.op (s i) := by
  rw [relElt]
  refine (map_sum
      (ConcreteCategory.hom ((tensorObj ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules) F).map f.op))
      _ _).trans
    (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_)
  refine (tensorObj_map_tmul (O := O.obj) ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules) F f.op
      ⟨relGen a (op U) (𝟙 U) i, relGen_mem a (op U) (𝟙 U) i⟩ (s i)).trans ?_
  exact congrArg
    (fun z : ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op V) ↦
      z ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op V)] F.map f.op (s i))
    (relSubmodule_map_relGen f a i)

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{max v w} RingCat.{max v w})] in
/-- The relation element is annihilated by the inclusion of the relation subpresheaf, tensored
with `F`.  This is where the relation `∑ a i • s i = 0` enters. -/
lemma tensorRight_map_ι_relElt {U : C} {n : ℕ}
    (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    {F : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)} (s : Fin n → F.obj (op U))
    (ha : ∑ i : Fin n, a i • s i = 0) :
    ((tensorRight F).map (relSubmodule a).ι).app (op U) (relElt a s) = 0 := by
  have hst : ∀ (r : (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)) (m : (freeOn O U).obj (op U))
      (y : F.obj (op U)),
      (r • m) ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)] y
        = m ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)] (r • y) :=
    fun _ _ _ ↦ TensorProduct.smul_tmul _ _ _
  have hts : ∀ (m : (freeOn O U).obj (op U)) (g : Fin n → F.obj (op U)),
      m ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)] (∑ i : Fin n, g i)
        = ∑ i : Fin n, m ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)] g i :=
    fun _ _ ↦ TensorProduct.tmul_sum _ _ _
  have htz : ∀ m : (freeOn O U).obj (op U),
      m ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)] (0 : F.obj (op U)) = 0 :=
    fun _ ↦ TensorProduct.tmul_zero _ _
  have key : ∀ i : Fin n,
      ((tensorRight F).map (relSubmodule a).ι).app (op U)
          ((⟨relGen a (op U) (𝟙 U) i, relGen_mem a (op U) (𝟙 U) i⟩ :
            ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op U))
              ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)] s i)
        = (ModuleCat.freeMk (ULift.up (𝟙 U) : (uliftYoneda.{w} U).obj (op U)) :
            (freeOn O U).obj (op U)) ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)] (a i • s i) := by
    intro i
    refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun z : (freeOn O U).obj (op U) ↦
      z ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)] s i) (relGen_id a i)) ?_
    exact hst _ _ _
  rw [relElt]
  refine (map_sum
      (ConcreteCategory.hom (((tensorRight F).map (relSubmodule a).ι).app (op U))) _ _).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ key i) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (hts _ (fun i ↦ a i • s i)).symm ?_
  rw [ha]
  exact htz _

end Element

section Criterion

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{max v w} RingCat.{max v w})]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max v w}]
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max v w}]
  {O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{max v w}}

/-- **Stacks 08FC, (1) implies (2).** -/
theorem hasLocalSingleRelationFactorizations_of_isFlat
    {F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)} (hF : IsFlat F) :
    HasLocalSingleRelationFactorizations O F := by
  intro U n a s ha
  have hinj := isLocallyInjective_tensorRight_map_of_isFlat hF (relSubmodule a).ι
    (Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_of_injective J _ fun X ↦
      PresheafOfModules.injective_of_mono (relSubmodule a).ι X)
  have hz : ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringPresheaf O.obj)).map
        ((tensorRightOf O F).map (relSubmodule a).ι)).app (op U) (relElt a s)
      = ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringPresheaf O.obj)).map
        ((tensorRightOf O F).map (relSubmodule a).ι)).app (op U) 0 := by
    rw [map_zero]
    exact tensorRight_map_ι_relElt a s ha
  have hS := Presheaf.equalizerSieve_mem J
    ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringPresheaf O.obj)).map
      ((tensorRightOf O F).map (relSubmodule a).ι)) (relElt a s) 0 hz
  refine ⟨_, hS, ?_⟩
  intro V f hf
  have hvan : (tensorObj ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules) (valR F)).map f.op (relElt a s)
      = 0 := Eq.trans hf (map_zero _)
  have hvan2 : ∑ i : Fin n, (⟨relGen a (op V) f i, relGen_mem a (op V) f i⟩ :
        ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op V))
          ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op V)] (valR F).map f.op (s i) = 0 :=
    (relElt_restrict f a s).symm.trans hvan
  obtain ⟨l, t, B, h1, h2⟩ := exists_relFactorization a (op V) f
    (fun i ↦ (valR F).map f.op (s i)) hvan2
  exact ⟨l, t, B, h1, fun k _ ↦ h2 k⟩

end Criterion

end Stacks.SheafOfModules
